From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=81ngel=20Ren=C3=A9?=
 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:27:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: s5p-mfc: v15 encoder: header with the first frame,
 bare VP8
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On MFC v15:

- default V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE to JOINED_WITH_1ST_FRAME.
  GStreamer expects one CAPTURE buffer per frame: with a separate header
  buffer it drops the next one, which is the keyframe.

- set bit 12 of E_VP8_OPTION. Without it the firmware wraps VP8 in IVF
  file and frame headers, and V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP8 is bare frames. Google's
  driver sets it too. There is then no header to return at sequence
  start, so on v15 do not return an empty buffer that would read as the
  end of the stream. Other versions return the header buffer as before.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c    | 22 ++++++++++++++++---
 .../platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c |  6 +++++
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
index 9b5d8449a..a8fde6456 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_enc.c
@@ -1172,7 +1172,13 @@ static int enc_post_seq_start(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx)
 	struct s5p_mfc_enc_params *p = &ctx->enc_params;
 	struct s5p_mfc_buf *dst_mb;
 
-	if (p->seq_hdr_mode == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_SEPARATE) {
+	/*
+	 * VP8 on v15 has no header (no IVF), so the stream size reads 0 here:
+	 * an empty buffer would look like the end of the stream.
+	 */
+	if (p->seq_hdr_mode == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_SEPARATE &&
+	    (!IS_MFCV15(dev) ||
+	     s5p_mfc_hw_call(dev->mfc_ops, get_enc_strm_size, dev))) {
 		if (!list_empty(&ctx->dst_queue)) {
 			dst_mb = list_entry(ctx->dst_queue.next,
 					struct s5p_mfc_buf, list);
@@ -2782,11 +2788,21 @@ int s5p_mfc_enc_ctrls_setup(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx)
 			if ((controls[i].type == V4L2_CTRL_TYPE_MENU) ||
 				(controls[i].type ==
 					V4L2_CTRL_TYPE_INTEGER_MENU)) {
+				s32 def = controls[i].default_value;
+
+				/*
+				 * On v15 the header comes with the first frame
+				 * by default: GStreamer expects one capture
+				 * buffer per frame and drops the extra one.
+				 */
+				if (controls[i].id ==
+				    V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE &&
+				    IS_MFCV15(ctx->dev))
+					def = V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_JOINED_WITH_1ST_FRAME;
 				ctx->ctrls[i] = v4l2_ctrl_new_std_menu(
 					&ctx->ctrl_handler,
 					&s5p_mfc_enc_ctrl_ops, controls[i].id,
-					controls[i].maximum, 0,
-					controls[i].default_value);
+					controls[i].maximum, 0, def);
 			} else {
 				ctx->ctrls[i] = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(
 					&ctx->ctrl_handler,
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
index 75a372e39..eaad16804 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/samsung/s5p-mfc/s5p_mfc_opr_v6.c
@@ -1650,6 +1650,12 @@ static int s5p_mfc_set_enc_params_vp8(struct s5p_mfc_ctx *ctx)
 	}
 	reg |= (val & 0xF) << 3;
 	reg |= (p_vp8->num_ref & 0x2);
+	/*
+	 * MFC v15 wraps VP8 in IVF (file and frame headers) unless bit 12 is
+	 * set; V4L2_PIX_FMT_VP8 is bare frames (Google's driver sets it too).
+	 */
+	if (IS_MFCV15(dev))
+		reg |= BIT(12);
 	writel(reg, mfc_regs->e_vp8_options);
 
 	mfc_debug_leave();
